{"name":"Shell Haven","hex":"#ebdfc0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Shell Haven","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A small bay and former port and oil refinery in Thurrock borough, Essex, England"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Shell_Haven"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shell Haven","blocks":[{"text":"Shell Haven was a port on the north bank of the Thames Estuary at the eastern end of Thurrock, Essex, England, and then an oil refinery. The refinery closed in 1999 and the site was purchased by DP World, who received planning consent in May 2007 for the new London Gateway deep-water container port at the site. The neighbouring Coryton Refinery remained in operation until 2012."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Shell_haven_191007.jpg/330px-Shell_haven_191007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shell_Haven"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Shell_Haven_refinery_1980.jpg/500px-Shell_Haven_refinery_1980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Shell_Haven_refinery_1980.jpg/1280px-Shell_Haven_refinery_1980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Shell_Haven_refinery_1980.jpg/500px-Shell_Haven_refinery_1980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shell Haven refinery tank farm 1980","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShell_Haven_refinery_1980.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Shell_Haven_oil_refinery.tif/lossless-page1-500px-Shell_Haven_oil_refinery.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/